at the error patterns across models, CLS consistently misses bugs at 75.5% while CWM generates false alarms at 83.1%, but an oracle ensemble combining both reaches 90.63% accuracy, which suggests complementary strengths worth exploiting.\n\nI'm structuring the paper around five core tables: dataset statistics first, then cross-model comparisons for both CLS and CWM at the repo level, followed by DeepSeek's function-level breakdown across the three formats, and finally re-repair resolution rates to close out the empirical findings.\n\nNow I need to account for the trajectory experiments at both repo and subset levels before diving into the writing.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6447,"cache_read_input_tokens":23703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6447},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d905b624-c5ef-406f-b658-55e6d1ececb7","uuid":"3db45542-471a-4221-9152-552d45b51eb6"}
